course: dictionary
lesson: 700
title: A tree that becomes a forest
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A banyan is a large tree from hot countries. Its branches send down roots. «A banyan drops roots from its branches that become new trunks.» So one tree can grow many trunks, and the picture in your head gets bigger.
explain: Use the clues around the word. «A banyan grows a forest of trunks» tells you the tree spreads out so far that it looks like a whole forest. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then test your idea in the sentence to see if it still makes sense.
explain: Some words are names for things you may not have seen. Banyan is one of them. The sentences around it describe what it does, so you can work out what kind of thing it is even before you check a dictionary.
explain: Dictionaries help when the clues are not enough. Read the dictionary meaning, then go back to the sentence and check that the meaning fits every clue.
fact: A banyan is a tropical fig tree from India.
fact: Its branches drop roots down to the ground, and those roots grow into new trunks.
fact: The banyan is the national tree of India.
fact: «The Great Banyan in Kolkata covers an area like a big park with thousands of root-trunks,» though its main trunk was removed in 1925.
fact: In stories and religion, people rest and meet under banyan trees, and Hindus and Buddhists see the tree as special.
exercise: What is a banyan? | A bird that lives in the desert | *A tropical fig tree from India | A kind of stone found in rivers
exercise: «A banyan drops roots from its branches that become new trunks.» What do the roots become? | Fruit | Leaves | *New trunks | Flowers
exercise: Why might a banyan look like a forest? | It only grows in dark caves | Many trees are planted close together in rows | It drops its leaves in a big pile | *It grows many trunks from its branches, so one tree looks like a whole forest
test: «The Great Banyan in Kolkata covers an area like a big park.» What does this tell you? | *One tree can spread over a very large area | Parks are made of banyan trees | A banyan is very small | Kolkata has no trees
test: Which country has the banyan as its national tree? | Japan | *India | Egypt | Brazil
exam: Based on «The banyan grows a forest of trunks», which is the best meaning of the sentence? | The banyan stores water in its fat trunk | The banyan has only one thin trunk | *One banyan tree can grow many trunks and look like a forest | The banyan is a forest of small bushes
